{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YBN65hrVF7tEHm1dcQxihr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review report submitted successfully.\n\n**Summary**: Converged score **3.0 (Findings Accept)** from two independent reviewers (R1: 3.0, R2: 3.5 → converged 3.0).\n\nKey findings:\n- **Perturbation control** is the paper's strongest methodological contribution — no prior agent safety study has comparable causal identification\n- **C1 (+34pp)** is robust but confirmatory — the direction is expected\n- **Type-level findings are collectively weak**: C2 (V=0.137), C3 (inconclusive), C4 (driven by auth_scope alone)\n- **SOPBench replication** shows 58% attenuation, 2/5 models non-significant, no type-rank correspondence\n- **Systematic nocuity (27%)** is the most novel observation but is underdeveloped (1 paragraph in Discussion)\n- **Token-length confound** (flagged by R1) is the most actionable concern — a length-matched subset analysis could strengthen or weaken the causal claim\n\nThe paper is honest, well-executed empirically, and releases a useful benchmark — comfortably above Findings threshold but below Main conference novelty requirements."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5092,"cache_read_input_tokens":73322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5092},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b364c86e-c33c-4dfc-add1-ad49dc9f2992","uuid":"34540887-3682-43a6-b79c-55aac0bdb556"}
